    "title": "Thunder vs Lakers injury report, prediction: Is Jalen Williams playing tonight?",
    "text": "Updated April 2, 2026, 7:31 p.m. CTThe OKC Thunder will be close to full strength when it hosts the Los Angeles Lakers at 8:30 p.m. CT Thursday.Jalen Williams and Isaiah Hartenstein are back for OKC (60-16) after not playing in its 114-110 overtime home win over the Detroit Pistons on Monday due to injury management. But Alex Caruso (illness) is listed as questionable.Los Angeles (50-26) continues to be without former Oklahoma State star Marcus Smart, who has missed the last five games due to a right ankle contusion. But that didn't stop the Lakers from earning a 127-113 home win over the Cleveland Cavaliers on Tuesday.Here's everything you need to know about Thursday's game between the Thunder and Lakers:Order our new book on Thunder's run to NBA title[ LISTEN UP: Make the \"Thunder Buddies\" podcast a staple of your starting lineup by following on Apple, Spotify and YouTube. ]What time is Thunder vs Lakers game tonight?Date: Thursday, April 2Time: 8:30 p.m. CTWhere: Paycom Center in Oklahoma CityWatch Thunder vs Lakers live on FuboWhat channel is OKC Thunder vs Los Angeles Lakers on tonight?Streaming: Prime Video (how to watch)Thunder vs Lakers predictions, picksJustin Martinez: OKC 117, Los Angeles 113Los Angeles is playing great basketball right now, and its defense has seemingly turned around. But it'll be tested against an OKC offense that has plenty of weapons. Shai Gilgeous-Alexander is one of the most unguardable players in basketball. Jalen Williams is a downhill threat. Chet Holmgren is a floor-spacing five. And the Thunder's bench has spark plugs such as Ajay Mitchell, Isaiah Joe, Jaylin Williams and Jared McCain. I think it'll all be too much for Los Angeles to contain, so give me OKC at home.Thunder vs Lakers betting oddsOdds via BetMGM as of Thursday, April 2Odds: Thunder by 8.5Over/under: 227.5Moneyline: OKC -350 | Los Angeles +280Thunder vs Lakers injury updatesThunder: Alex Caruso (illness) is questionable. Thomas Sorber (right ACL surgical recovery) is out.Lakers: Kobe Bufkin (G League assignment) is out. Dalton Knecht (G League assignment) is out. Marcus Smart (right ankle contusion) is out. Adou Thiero (G League assignment) is out.Projected OKC Thunder startersShai Gilgeous-AlexanderJalen WilliamsLu DortChet HolmgrenIsaiah HartensteinProjected Los Angeles Lakers startersLuka DoncicAustin ReavesJake LaRaviaLeBron JamesDeandre AytonJustin Martinez covers the Thunder and NBA for The Oklahoman. Have a story idea for Justin? He can be reached at jmartinez@oklahoman.com or on X/Twitter at @Justintohoops. Sign up for the Thunder Sports Minute newsletter to access more NBA coverage. Support Justin's work and that of other Oklahoman journalists by purchasing a digital subscription today at subscribe.oklahoman.com.Our editors independently choose our recommendations. Some content is produced with paid support from a third party, however our editorial decisions remain independent. If you buy through our links, the USA TODAY Network may earn a commission. Prices and availability may change.",
